※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4595

※ What `@[external]` may name is what the runtime packaged with the compiler
※ defines; there is no linker and nothing else to reach.  A name that is not one
※ of those is a call to something that will not be there, which is worth saying
※ where it is written rather than leaving to whatever reads the image.

@[external("no_such_thing")]
fn missing() → i64

@[startup, impure]
fn main() → u6:
    if missing() = 0i64: 0u6 else: 1u6
